Slack platform / — / — / https://api.slack.com
  (external service; the Slack Web API is consumed at runtime over HTTPS and the
  chat app is created from src/ne/chat/slack/manifest.json — nothing is
  distributed with this package, no Slack SDK is embedded. slack_sdk / slack-bolt
  were deliberately NOT adopted: their own urllib/aiohttp transport stacks would
  bypass the C2 egress import allowlist and the mandated httpx.MockTransport
  fixture-first CI, so a thin httpx client is used instead — the merged NE-045
  build-vs-adopt precedent. This mirrors the Keycloak external-service note in
  ne-identity/NOTICE.)

FastAPI and its transitive Starlette are embedded Python dependencies. httpx is
the WRITE-side Slack Web API client transport (and the TestClient transport).
Slack is an external service. No Slack SDK is embedded or distributed.

Microsoft Bot Framework / Azure Bot Service / — / — / https://dev.botframework.com
  (external service; the Bot Framework Connector REST API is consumed at runtime
  over HTTPS and inbound activity JWTs are validated against the OpenID metadata
  at login.botframework.com — nothing is distributed with this package. NO
  botbuilder / Microsoft 365 Agents SDK is embedded: the Bot Framework SDK was
  archived Dec 2025 and the M365 Agents SDK migration guidance itself delegates
  inbound auth to plain JWT validation left to the host, so a thin first-party
  httpx client implements the documented REST wire protocol — the same
  build-vs-adopt call NE-045 made for slack_sdk. PyJWT + cryptography above are
  already repo-locked via ne-connect/ne-identity, so this adds no new lock entry.)
